<div class="gask"><b>Her Exam 1 hints</b><ul><li>&ldquo;The drugs in each pharmacological class (know the drug table); The general mechanism of action for each drug class. This includes being able to explain why that MOA is good for treating the skin conditions it is indicated for.; The details of the MOAs differentiate the drugs within the class; ... Know Black Box warning adverse drug reactions&rdquo;.</li><li>&ldquo;Know what the drugs target.&rdquo; Fill-in-the-blanks focus on drug mechanisms. She asks with generic names only (10/29, T 618&ndash;621).</li></ul></div>

