<div class="g2-clsgrid"><div class="g2-cls g2-c2"><div class="g2-cls-h"><span class="g2-cls-t">Alcaftadine versus cetirizine</span></div><div class="g2-stats"><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">Both</span><span class="g2-stat-v">Low anticholinergic and CNS effects</span></div><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">Cetirizine only</span><span class="g2-stat-v">Can still cause drowsiness</span></div></div></div><div class="g2-cls g2-c2"><div class="g2-cls-h"><span class="g2-cls-t">Azelastine versus the others</span></div><div class="g2-stats"><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">Azelastine</span><span class="g2-stat-v">Some anticholinergic activity and CNS penetration</span></div><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">Cetirizine, alcaftadine</span><span class="g2-stat-v">Minimal or very little of each</span></div></div></div></div>
