<div class="g2-note"><span class="g2-k">What causes angle closure</span><div class="g2-stats"><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">Slide</span><span class="g2-stat-v">The shape of the eye and how it sits in the socket (she repeated it, 11/13 T@20737)</span></div><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">Lecture example</span><span class="g2-stat-v">A blow to the eye with swelling, or a chemical exposure, after which the iris sticks and the exit closes (11/13 T@23787)</span></div><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">Key</span><span class="g2-stat-v">The shape of the eye (slide and her direct statement)</span></div><div class="g2-stat"><span class="g2-stat-k">The injury</span><span class="g2-stat-v">An example of how closure occurs</span></div></div></div>
