<details class="g2-self"><summary>Provide counseling points on the administration of carbamide peroxide 6.5% otic drops. <span class="g2-tap">Show answer</span></summary><p>5&ndash;10 drops in the affected ear; keep them in for several minutes, a cotton ball may hold them; twice daily for up to 4 days; remaining wax is removed by gentle warm-water irrigation with a rubber otic bulb syringe; contact the PCP if symptoms persist after 4 days <span class="g2-src">(Lam Otic slide 14, 16, 44)</span><span class="g2-src">(Lam Otic handout p. 9)</span>.</p></details>
