<div class="gpt g2-block"><h5 id="lt4-6"><span class="g2-num">5.</span> Mix-ups: 4 days versus 7 days, adult versus child technique <span class="g2-src"><span class="g2-src">(Lam Otic slide 16, 33, 34)</span></span></h5><details class="g2-fold"><summary><span class="g2-fold-s">Show this section</span></summary><p class="g2-p g2-capline">Intervals and positions in ear-drop counseling.</p><table class="g2-table g2-kv"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Adult</th><td>Lie with the affected ear up; pull the earlobe out and up <span class="g2-src">(Lam Otic slide 33)</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Child under 3</th><td>Pull the ear back and down <span class="g2-src">(Lam Otic slide 33)</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Impaction: contact the PCP</th><td>If symptoms persist after 4 days <span class="g2-src">(Lam Otic slide 16)</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Water-clogged ear: see a PCP</th><td>No benefit after several days printed; 7 days said aloud <span class="g2-src">T@100232 11/20</span></td></tr></tbody></table></details></div>
